// Dungeons (GDD, section 11), in order of difficulty: Rune Golem (Wind), Wyvern Nest (Fire), Bone King's Crypt
// (Dark), Drowned Sanctum (Water) and the Cracked Forge (Light). Each one is mostly its element, so the team that
// beats it is the one with the advantage (Fire, Water, Light, Wind, Dark). They open during the Campaign, but the
// Golem floor 1 is about stage 35, and the next Dungeon's floor 5 always asks more than the last one's: Golem 5 right
// after the Campaign, the Forge 5 only with 6★ level 40, 6★ +15 runes, Awakening and skills maxed. Enemies go past
// 6★ level 40, up to 60, and "scale" multiplies their HP and Attack (the calibration of each floor).
// Each victory costs the floor's Mana ("mana"); a defeat costs nothing.
// Each Dungeon has its own team. "firstClearGold" is the Gold of the first victory on the floor. Rune
// Dungeons drop 4 to 6 star runes only from their four sets, with a minimum rarity per floor; the Forge
// drops Grindstones and Enchanted Gems (grade 1 Magic ... 4 Legendary).
// Every victory drops the loot. "unlockStage" is the Campaign stage that opens the Dungeon.
